From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:54:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wlan-faster-boot: load wlan after firmware setup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

boot.kernelModules loaded the prima wlan module at sysinit, before
wlan-firmware-hoki.service symlinked the vendor firmware and powered WCNSS
up, so every boot waited ~10 s for WCNSS, failed with "No such device",
and held sysinit.target for that time — a pure stall, since the module is
loaded again later by wlan-firmware-hoki.service. Drop the early load;
Wi-Fi still comes up via wlan-firmware-hoki.service and boot is ~5 s
shorter.
---
 devices/fossil-hoki/wlan.nix | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/devices/fossil-hoki/wlan.nix b/devices/fossil-hoki/wlan.nix
index 18d05338..10b15f15 100644
--- a/devices/fossil-hoki/wlan.nix
+++ b/devices/fossil-hoki/wlan.nix
@@ -105,8 +105,10 @@ let
   };
 in
 {
-  # wlan-firmware-hoki.sh symlinks the vendor firmware and opens
-  # /dev/wcnss_wlan before this module is loaded.
+  # wlan-firmware-hoki.sh symlinks the vendor firmware, powers WCNSS up and
+  # loads this module itself. Do not also list it in boot.kernelModules:
+  # systemd-modules-load runs before those symlinks exist, so the prima probe
+  # waits ~10 s for WCNSS, fails with "No such device", and holds
+  # sysinit.target (and therefore the whole boot) for that time.
   boot.extraModulePackages = [ wlanModule ];
-  boot.kernelModules = [ "wlan" ];
 }
